desc: Spectral Vowel Morpher v2 - voice<->wash capture instrument
// =====================================================================
// Capture-based vocal instrument. Feeds on LIVE audio playing into it (drag a
// WAV onto the track, or send another track in -- the proper REAPER way).
// Capture a moment into a slot; it's analyzed two ways at once:
//   * harmonic (voice) -- pitch-detected additive resynth: keeps the vowel
//   * spectral (wash)   -- PaulStretch-style phase randomization: breathy bed
// TEXTURE crossfades between them (0 = voice, 100 = wash). Capture up to 8
// slots and MORPH between them. Captures persist across save/reopen.
//
// USE: put audio on the track. Input level up / Voice down -> you hear source.
// When you hear the moment, hit Capture. (Then sweep CAPTURE POINT by ear to
// land exactly on the vowel -- it re-analyzes live, compensating for the
// fraction of a second between hearing and pressing.) Pull Input down, Voice
// up, set Texture, and Morph between slots.
//
//   Capture point = where in the grab to analyze (0 = earliest .. 100 = at press).
//                   PER SLOT: each slot remembers its own point, so scrubbing one
//                   slot never retunes the others. Switching Capture slot shows
//                   that slot's saved point.
//   Texture       = 0 voice (harmonic) .. 100 wash (phase-randomized)
//   Wash grain   = short = rough/grainy, long = glassy/smooth (wash character)
//   Spread        = spectral blur (Hz);  Audition = monitor focused slot / morph
//   Auto-morph    = Off / Sweep (back+forth) / Glide once (first->last slot) / Shuffle (random-order wander)
//   Drift         = suite-wide automation replacement: pick a parameter, and it
//                   wanders on its own (up/down amounts + a wall-clock period),
//                   so a mouse-free / screen-reader user gets evolving motion
//                   without drawing REAPER automation. All targets drift at once.
// =====================================================================

// --- Controls are grouped by what they belong to, not by when they were added.
//     Renumbered THREE times during v2's build: at birth, when Slot crossfade
//     was added, and when Slot mute joined the group. Renumbering is free while
//     the plugin has no shipped saved projects -- breathing_v2.rpp regenerates
//     from breathing.rpp via tools/morpher_v1_to_v2.py, which maps by label
//     rather than by slider number. Once v2 is shipped and other people have
//     projects using it, IDs become primary keys and additions append. Until
//     then, getting the layout right is the goal, not preserving numbers. ---
slider1:0<0,7,1>Capture slot
slider2:0<0,1,1{Off,Capture now}>Capture spectrum
slider3:0<0,100,1>Capture point (per slot: earliest .. at press)
// Slot linger: PER SLOT, edited for whichever Capture slot is selected -- the
// same nested-selector shape as the per-slot Capture point above, and placed
// next to it so everything belonging to the selected slot sits together.
//
// It is the PURE HOLD TIME for this slot, in seconds -- how long you hear this
// slot alone before its crossfade to the next slot begins. Slot crossfade
// (below) adds fade time ON TOP of this: total time on the slot = linger +
// crossfade. That means the number you type IS what you hear: linger 4 = 4
// seconds of hearing this slot alone. No arithmetic to figure out hold from
// some other value.
//
// linger 0 means "no hold, all crossfade" (matches the original Morpher's
// continuous-morph behaviour when paired with a non-zero crossfade).
slider4:4<0,300,0.1>Slot linger (sec) (per slot: pure hold time you hear this slot alone)

// --- Slot crossfade: PER SLOT, placed beside Slot linger where it belongs.
//     Adds fade time AFTER the linger's pure hold, so the fade transitions
//     from this slot to the next one. Total time on this slot's leg =
//     linger + crossfade. Set to 0 for a hard cut at the end of the hold;
//     set to any positive value for a smooth transition to the next slot. ---
slider5:1<0,300,0.1>Slot crossfade (sec) (per slot: fade to next slot, added after the hold)

// --- Slot mute: PER SLOT, appended at slider6 (slider IDs are primary keys
//     now, so this stays at the end). When On, the slot is skipped in Sweep /
//     Glide / Shuffle -- the morph moves directly to the next unmuted slot,
//     with no crossfade to nothing in between. Focused mode ignores mute (it
//     always plays the slot you point at, that's what Focused is for). Set
//     once per slot via the Capture slot selector; a captured silence slot
//     between two audio slots is the canonical use, so the morph fades sound
//     to sound rather than sound to silence to sound. ---
slider6:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>Slot mute (per slot: skip in morph)
slider7:0<-60,12,0.1>Input level (dry, dB)
slider8:0<-60,12,0.1>Voice level (dB)
slider9:50<0,100,1>Texture (0 voice, 100 wash)
slider10:150<5,680,1>Wash grain (ms)
slider11:0<0,150,0.5>Spread (Hz)
slider12:0<-24,24,0.1>Pitch (semitones)
slider13:50<0,100,1>Stereo width
slider14:0<0,500,1>Low cut (Hz)
slider15:0<0,100,0.1>Denoise
slider16:1<0,1,1{Focused slot,Morph}>Audition
slider17:0<0,100,0.1>Morph (across captured slots)
slider18:0<0,3,1{Off,Sweep (back+forth),Glide once,Shuffle (random)}>Auto-morph
// --- Drift: suite-wide automation replacement (nested-selector pattern).
//     Pick a target; it wanders by up/down amounts over a wall-clock period.
//     All targets drift in parallel; the selector only chooses which one the
//     amount/period/shape sliders are editing. Added at the END of the range
//     (slider IDs are primary keys — never renumber existing ones). ---
slider19:0<0,8,1{Texture,Spread,Pitch,Stereo width,Low cut,Voice level,Denoise,Morph,Input level}>Drift target
slider20:0<0,300,0.1>Drift up amount (units match target)
slider21:0<0,300,0.1>Drift down amount (units match target)
slider22:30<1,600,0.5>Drift period (seconds)
slider23:0<0,2,1{Sine,Triangle,Random}>Drift shape
// Restart on play = drift jumps to the start of its cycle when the transport
// begins (so multiple tracks reset together and stay in sync). Free-running =
// drift ignores the transport and evolves continuously (loop under/over an
// unbroken drift). A loop repeat is never a restart in either mode.
slider24:0<0,1,1{Restart on play,Free-running}>Drift restart
// --- Ramp: the suite's "Speed Ramp" under an honest name (this plugin has no
//     speed to ramp). A one-time slow RIDE of a parameter: pick a target, how
//     far to move it (signed) and over how long, arm Engage, and it glides there
//     once and holds. Nested-selector like Drift; all targets ride in parallel
//     off one Engage; composes with Drift (base + drift wander + ramp ride). ---
slider25:0<0,8,1{Texture,Spread,Pitch,Stereo width,Low cut,Voice level,Denoise,Morph,Input level}>Ramp target
slider26:0<-300,300,0.1>Ramp by (units match target)
slider27:0<0,60,0.1>Ramp duration (minutes)
slider28:0<0,60,0.1>Ramp start delay (minutes)
slider29:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>Ramp engage

@init
// ext_noinit = 1: @init runs ONLY on plugin load, so captured slots (and all
// memory) survive transport stop/play -- the whole point of a capture-based
// instrument. RUNTIME state (accumulators, positions, smoother) is reset
// explicitly on the transport play-edge in @block instead, so playback still
// restarts cleanly (and renders correctly) without wiping the captures.
ext_noinit = 1;
TWOPI = 6.283185307179586; PI = 3.141592653589793;
NSLOTS = 8; MAXFFT = 32768; INRING = 65536;
N_TARGETS = 9;   // Texture, Spread, Pitch, Stereo width, Low cut, Voice level, Denoise, Morph, Input level
// Wash grain is deliberately NOT a target: it rebuilds a window rather than
// scaling a value, so it is driven from @block and cannot read a per-sample
// drift offset the way the others do.
FFTSIZE = 32768; NBINS = 16385;
// WA = analysis window length, FIXED and decoupled from Wash grain. The capture
// analysis (heavy: FFT + YIN) happens at WA; Wash grain only rebuilds the cheap
// synthesis grain. That makes Wash grain safe to AUTOMATE (no re-FFT, no buffer
// clear -> no dropouts), and Capture point scrubs this WA-length window in the grab.
WA = 8192;   // ~170 ms @ 48k: good spectral resolution, leaves ~0.5 s scrub range
// ACCLEN must exceed the LONGEST grain (W up to MAXFFT) plus a hop, or a long
// grain wraps the circular accumulator onto the read pointer (audible at the
// top of the Window-size range). 2*MAXFFT is comfortable headroom.
ACCLEN = 65536;
NHARM = 64; WHARM = 3072;          // 64 harmonics; ~64 ms YIN analysis window
WTBL = 8192; WTSCALE = WTBL / TWOPI;
// Voice stereo width: at full Stereo width the right-channel voice runs +-0.8%
// (~14 cents) detuned from the left, so L/R beat slowly -> width + de-robot
// shimmer. Tune by ear; bigger = wider/chorus-ier, smaller = tighter.
VOICE_DETUNE_MAX = 0.008;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Memory map: a RUNNING allocator, not hand-picked addresses. Every buffer is
// sized from the constants above, so NSLOTS (or any window size) can change
// without hand-editing offsets. The old fixed-address map collided the moment
// NSLOTS went past 4 (slotraw ran straight into slot_norm) -- this cannot.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
freemem = 0;
fftwork   = freemem; freemem += 2*FFTSIZE;    // FFT scratch (interleaved re/im)
inbuf     = freemem; freemem += INRING;        // live input ring
window    = freemem; freemem += WA;            // Hann of length WA (fixed analysis window)
synwin    = freemem; freemem += MAXFFT;        // sqrt-Hann synthesis grain (length W = Wash grain)
accL      = freemem; freemem += ACCLEN;        // overlap-add accumulator L
accR      = freemem; freemem += ACCLEN;        // overlap-add accumulator R
mtmp      = freemem; freemem += NBINS;
curmag    = freemem; freemem += NBINS;
phase     = freemem; freemem += NBINS;
doff      = freemem; freemem += NBINS;         // per-bin stereo decorrelation offsets
grainbuf  = freemem; freemem += MAXFFT;
// --- per-slot capture stores (ALL sized by NSLOTS -- this is what makes the
//     slot count a free dial) ---
slotmag   = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS*NBINS;  // wash (spectral) magnitudes
slotraw   = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS*MAXFFT; // raw captured audio (source of truth)
slot_norm = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;        // wash peak normalization
slot_harm = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS*NHARM;  // voice harmonic magnitudes
slot_f0   = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;        // detected fundamentals (Hz)
slot_hnorm= freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;        // voice peak normalization
slot_voicedb  = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;   // PER-SLOT voice_db_base
slot_texture  = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;   // PER-SLOT texture
slot_spread   = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;   // PER-SLOT spread_hz
slot_pitch    = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;   // PER-SLOT pitch_semi
slot_width    = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;   // PER-SLOT stereo_width
slot_lowcut   = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;   // PER-SLOT lowcut_hz
slot_denoise  = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;   // PER-SLOT denoise_amt
slot_linger   = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;      // PER-SLOT step time in SECONDS (time to leave this slot)
slot_xfade    = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;      // PER-SLOT crossfade length in SECONDS; hold = linger - xfade
slot_mute     = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;      // PER-SLOT mute flag (0/1); muted slots are skipped in Sweep / Glide / Shuffle
active_slots  = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;      // indices of unmuted slots (0..n_used-1 minus muted ones); rebuilt every @block
slot_cappoint = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;    // PER-SLOT capture point (0..1): where in each slot's grab to analyze. Each slot remembers its own scrub position.
// --- harmonic (voice) engine scratch ---
hph       = freemem; freemem += NHARM;         // resynth phase accumulators (voice A, left)
hphB      = freemem; freemem += NHARM;         // resynth phase accumulators (voice B, left)
hphR      = freemem; freemem += NHARM;         // voice A, right channel (detuned for width)
hphBR     = freemem; freemem += NHARM;         // voice B, right channel (detuned for width)
anbuf     = freemem; freemem += WHARM;         // mono analysis frame
yin_df    = freemem; freemem += WHARM;         // YIN difference function
yin_cmnd  = freemem; freemem += WHARM;         // YIN cumulative-mean-normalized difference
// --- sine wavetable (render-speed optimization): the voice engine's per-sample
// sin() calls become a table lookup. Internal only -- no sliders, no pitch or
// behavior change (frequency is set by the phase INCREMENT, which is untouched). ---
sintab    = freemem; freemem += WTBL+2;        // one sine period + a guard sample for interp
driftbag  = freemem; freemem += NSLOTS;        // Auto-morph Shuffle bag (even random slot coverage)
// --- suite Drift: per-target config + runtime banks (16-slot-spaced for growth) ---
target_drift_up     = freemem; freemem += 16;  // CONFIG: up amount   (survives transport)
target_drift_down   = freemem; freemem += 16;  // CONFIG: down amount
target_drift_per    = freemem; freemem += 16;  // CONFIG: period (seconds)
target_drift_shape  = freemem; freemem += 16;  // CONFIG: 0 Sine / 1 Triangle / 2 Random
target_drift_phase  = freemem; freemem += 16;  // RUNTIME: 0..1 phase (reset on play)
target_drift_prev   = freemem; freemem += 16;  // RUNTIME: Random shape prev value
target_drift_curr   = freemem; freemem += 16;  // RUNTIME: Random shape target value
target_drift_offset = freemem; freemem += 16;  // RUNTIME: current offset (read at consumption)
td_active           = freemem; freemem += 16;  // @slider: 1 if a target has any drift configured
// --- Ramp: per-target config + runtime banks (16-slot-spaced) ---
ramp_by_mem            = freemem; freemem += 16;  // CONFIG: signed `by` amount
ramp_dur_mem           = freemem; freemem += 16;  // CONFIG: duration (minutes)
ramp_delay_mem         = freemem; freemem += 16;  // CONFIG: start delay (minutes)
ramp_t_mem             = freemem; freemem += 16;  // RUNTIME: 0..1 ride progress (reset on play)
ramp_delay_elapsed_mem = freemem; freemem += 16;  // RUNTIME: start-delay sample counter
ramp_offset_mem        = freemem; freemem += 16;  // RUNTIME: ramp_t * by (read at consumption)
mod_active             = freemem; freemem += 16;  // @slider: 1 if a target has drift OR ramp configured
i = 0; loop(WTBL+1, sintab[i] = sin(TWOPI*i/WTBL); i += 1; );
// captured slots persist across transport play (one-time init)
slots_inited == 0 ? (
  slots_inited = 1;
  i = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_norm[i] = 1; slot_cappoint[i] = 0; slot_linger[i] = 4; slot_xfade[i] = 1; slot_mute[i] = 0; slot_voicedb[i] = 0.0; slot_texture[i] = 0.5; slot_spread[i] = 0.0; slot_pitch[i] = 0.0; slot_width[i] = 50.0; slot_lowcut[i] = 0.0; slot_denoise[i] = 0.0; i += 1; );  // per-slot capture point defaults to 0 (earliest); @serialize restores/migrates
  i = 0; loop(NBINS, doff[i] = rand(1)*2 - 1; i += 1; );
  // have / n_used live in this ONE-TIME guard so captures survive transport
  // play (@init re-runs on every play; if these were reset there, a capture
  // made in one play would be orphaned on the next).
  have = 0; n_used = 0;
  // Drift CONFIG defaults live in the same one-time guard, for the same reason:
  // they must survive transport play. @serialize overwrites these with the
  // saved config on project load (the guard runs on fresh load, BEFORE the
  // @serialize restore — the exact order the captures above already rely on).
  i = 0; loop(N_TARGETS,
    target_drift_up[i]    = 0;
    target_drift_down[i]  = 0;
    target_drift_per[i]   = 30;
    target_drift_shape[i] = 0;
    ramp_by_mem[i]    = 0;   // Ramp CONFIG defaults (same one-time-guard rationale)
    ramp_dur_mem[i]   = 0;   // 0 duration = ramp inert until the user sets it
    ramp_delay_mem[i] = 0;
    i += 1;
  );
  last_target_select = 0;
  last_ramp_target   = 0;
  last_cap_slot      = 0;   // per-slot Capture-point selector (mirrors the Drift/Ramp target selectors)
);
// Drift RUNTIME state (phase/prev/curr/offset) is reset here on load AND on the
// transport play-edge in @block, so drift restarts at phase 0 on every play
// (continues across stop) — matching the rest of the suite.
i = 0; loop(N_TARGETS,
  target_drift_phase[i] = 0; target_drift_prev[i] = 0;
  target_drift_curr[i]  = 0; target_drift_offset[i] = 0;
  ramp_t_mem[i] = 0; ramp_delay_elapsed_mem[i] = 0; ramp_offset_mem[i] = 0;
  i += 1;
);
eff_spread_hz = 0; eff_lowcut_hz = 0; eff_stereo_width = 0;   // seeded properly in @slider/@sample
// runtime state
cap_last = 0; first_slider = 1; inpos = 0; last_gsamp = -1; last_cappoint = 0;
cap_dirty = 0; settle = 0;   // debounce for Capture-point re-analysis
// Captured spectra re-derive LAZILY -- only when actually stale (a fresh project
// load, or a capture-point scrub), never on an ordinary stop/play. In the normal
// capture-then-play flow nothing re-derives at all. Starts stale on load
// (@serialize restores the raw audio but not the analysis derived from it).
analysis_valid = 0;
rms_smooth = 0;   // slow auto-gain state (stable loudness, no per-grain pump)
cap_point01 = 0;  // analysis position in the grab (slider3); 0 = earliest
texture = 0.5; hlevel = 0.707; wlevel = 0.707;   // voice<->wash crossfade
i = 0; loop(NHARM, hph[i] = rand(1)*TWOPI; hphB[i] = rand(1)*TWOPI; hphR[i] = hph[i]; hphBR[i] = hphB[i]; i += 1; );
voice_detune = 0;   // right-channel voice detune amount (from Stereo width)
i = 0; loop(WA, window[i] = 0.5 - 0.5*cos(TWOPI*i/(WA-1)); i += 1; );   // analysis window (fixed)
morph_phase = 0; eff_morph01 = 0; last_automode = -1; last_ps = 0;
drift_was_playing = 0;   // Drift restart-on-play edge state
cur_slot = 0; nxt_slot = 0; xfade = 0;             // Drift: direct crossfade cur_slot -> nxt_slot
bag_pos = 999; last_slot = 0; drift_primed = 0; auto_primed = 0; sweep_dir = 1; leg_elapsed = 0;   // walk + shuffle-bag state (primed lazily in @sample)
// Fresh instance: every slot starts as whatever is on screen. Without this only
// the slot selected when a slider was last touched would carry the visible
// settings, and the others would sit at hard-coded defaults.
seed_slots_from_sliders = 1;
// Scramble the RNG per load: EEL rand() otherwise replays the SAME sequence
// every session, so Drift would wander the identical path each time you open the
// project. Advance it a sub-second-time-dependent number of steps so each load
// starts somewhere different. One-time, bounded, ~free.
_tp = time_precise(); i = 0; loop(floor(1 + (_tp - floor(_tp)) * 500), rand(1); i += 1; );

// grab the most recent MAXFFT input samples into a slot's raw store
function grab_raw(slot) local(i, idx, base) (
  base = slot*MAXFFT;
  i = 0;
  loop(MAXFFT, idx = inpos - MAXFFT + i; idx < 0 ? idx += INRING; slotraw[base+i] = inbuf[idx]; i += 1; );
);

// FFT WA samples of a slot's raw, Hann-windowed, zero-padded to FFTSIZE. Uses the
// FIXED analysis window WA (not the synthesis grain W), so Wash grain never
// triggers this. Capture point picks WHERE in the ~0.68 s grab to look: 0 =
// earliest (the sustained vowel, since you react a beat after hearing it) .. 1 =
// the press-moment.
function compute_spectrum(slot) local(i, re, im, mx, rbase, mbase) (
  rbase = slot*MAXFFT + floor(slot_cappoint[slot] * (MAXFFT - WA)); mbase = slot*NBINS;   // per-slot capture point
  i = 0; loop(WA, fftwork[2*i] = slotraw[rbase+i]*window[i]; fftwork[2*i+1] = 0; i += 1; );
  i = WA; loop(FFTSIZE - WA, fftwork[2*i] = 0; fftwork[2*i+1] = 0; i += 1; );
  fft(fftwork, FFTSIZE); fft_permute(fftwork, FFTSIZE);
  mx = 0; i = 0;
  loop(NBINS,
    re = fftwork[2*i]; im = fftwork[2*i+1];
    slotmag[mbase+i] = sqrt(re*re + im*im);
    slotmag[mbase+i] > mx ? mx = slotmag[mbase+i];
    i += 1;
  );
  slot_norm[slot] = mx > 0 ? mx : 1;
);

// YIN-lite pitch detect (+ subharmonic octave fix) then 64 harmonic magnitudes
// (direct DFT). VOICE end of the Texture knob -- harmonics at the exact detected
// f0 avoid the bin-drift that wrecks phase-coherent resynth from a frozen frame.
function analyze_harm(slot) local(base, ci, almin, almax, tmax, tau, ii, d, dd, run, thr, res, cand, lockon, best, pa, pb, pc, pden, psh, f0d, hn, hf, kk, re, im, ang, hannv, mag, mx, boff) (
  base = slot*MAXFFT + floor(slot_cappoint[slot] * (MAXFFT - WHARM));   // same per-slot point as the wash
  ci = 0; loop(WHARM, anbuf[ci] = slotraw[base+ci]; ci += 1; );
  almin = floor(srate/600); almax = ceil(srate/70); tmax = min(2*almax, WHARM-1);
  tau = 1;
  loop(tmax, d = 0; ii = 0; loop(WHARM - tmax, dd = anbuf[ii] - anbuf[ii+tau]; d += dd*dd; ii += 1; ); yin_df[tau] = d; tau += 1; );
  yin_cmnd[0] = 1; run = 0; tau = 1;
  loop(tmax, run += yin_df[tau]; yin_cmnd[tau] = yin_df[tau]*tau/(run+0.000001); tau += 1; );
  thr = 0.15; res = -1; cand = -1; lockon = 0; tau = almin;
  loop(almax - almin,
    res < 0 ? ( lockon == 0 ? ( yin_cmnd[tau] < thr ? ( lockon = 1; cand = tau; ); )
                            : ( yin_cmnd[tau] < yin_cmnd[cand] ? ( cand = tau; ) : ( res = cand; ); ); );
    tau += 1;
  );
  (res < 0 && lockon == 1) ? res = cand;
  res < 0 ? ( best = 1000000000; tau = almin; loop(almax - almin, yin_cmnd[tau] < best ? ( best = yin_cmnd[tau]; res = tau; ); tau += 1; ); );
  loop(3, (2*res <= tmax && yin_cmnd[2*res] < 0.25 && yin_cmnd[2*res] < 1.15*yin_cmnd[res]) ? res = 2*res; );
  (res > 1 && res < tmax) ? ( pa = yin_cmnd[res-1]; pb = yin_cmnd[res]; pc = yin_cmnd[res+1]; pden = pa-2*pb+pc; psh = (pden!=0)?0.5*(pa-pc)/pden:0; ) : ( psh = 0; );
  f0d = srate/(res+psh);
  (f0d > 20 && f0d < srate*0.5) ? (
    boff = slot*NHARM; mx = 0; hn = 1;
    loop(NHARM,
      hf = hn*f0d;
      hf < srate*0.5 ? (
        re = 0; im = 0; kk = 0;
        loop(WHARM, hannv = 0.5 - 0.5*cos(TWOPI*kk/(WHARM-1)); ang = TWOPI*hf*kk/srate; re += anbuf[kk]*hannv*cos(ang); im -= anbuf[kk]*hannv*sin(ang); kk += 1; );
        mag = sqrt(re*re + im*im);
      ) : ( mag = 0; );
      slot_harm[boff + (hn-1)] = mag; mag > mx ? mx = mag; hn += 1;
    );
    slot_f0[slot] = f0d; slot_hnorm[slot] = mx > 0 ? mx : 1;
  );
);

function capture(slot) (
  grab_raw(slot);
  slot_cappoint[slot] = cap_point01;   // stamp this slot with the current capture point; scrubbing later re-tunes only this slot
  compute_spectrum(slot);   // wash (spectral) analysis
  analyze_harm(slot);       // voice (harmonic) analysis -- same captured frame
  have = 1;
  (slot + 1) > n_used ? n_used = slot + 1;
);

function build_spectrum(useR) local(i, srcb, b0, fr, m, ph, woff, re, im, mir) (
  woff = eff_stereo_width * 0.01 * PI;   // eff_ = base + Drift offset (set per-sample)
  // Build a Hermitian-symmetric spectrum so ifft() returns a REAL signal:
  // fill bins 0..N/2 from the magnitude data, mirror them as conjugates.
  i = 0;
  loop(GBINS,
    // GR maps this grain's bin grid back onto the fixed analysis grid, so the
    // same frequency is read whatever size the synthesis FFT currently is.
    srcb = i * GR / pitch_ratio;
    (srcb >= 0 && srcb < NBINS - 1) ? ( b0 = floor(srcb); fr = srcb - b0; m = (curmag[b0]*(1-fr) + curmag[b0+1]*fr) * GINV; ) : ( m = 0; );
    ph = phase[i] + (useR ? woff*doff[i] : 0);
    re = m * cos(ph); im = m * sin(ph);
    fftwork[2*i] = re; fftwork[2*i+1] = im;
    (i > 0 && i < GFFT/2) ? ( mir = GFFT - i; fftwork[2*mir] = re; fftwork[2*mir+1] = -im; );
    i += 1;
  );
  fftwork[1] = 0;                       // DC imaginary = 0
  fftwork[2*(GFFT/2)+1] = 0;            // Nyquist imaginary = 0
  fft_ipermute(fftwork, GFFT);
  ifft(fftwork, GFFT);
);

function gen_grain() local(i, j, si, sj, mfr, ni, nj, bi, bj, sp, sumv, cnt, bj2, pk, thr, cutbin, sv, rms, gnorm, aw) (
  // slot selection (vsi/vsj/vmfr) is computed once per sample in @sample so the
  // wash and the harmonic voice always agree on which slot(s) they're playing.
  si = vsi; sj = vsj; mfr = vmfr;
  ni = slot_norm[si]; ni <= 0 ? ni = 1;
  nj = slot_norm[sj]; nj <= 0 ? nj = 1;
  bi = si*NBINS; bj = sj*NBINS;
  i = 0;
  loop(NBINS, mtmp[i] = (1-mfr)*(slotmag[bi+i]/ni) + mfr*(slotmag[bj+i]/nj); i += 1; );
  sp = floor(eff_spread_hz * FFTSIZE / srate);   // eff_ = base + Drift offset
  // Spread is a box blur across frequency bins. It used to re-add every
  // neighbour from scratch for each bin, so its cost grew with the width -- at
  // Spread 100 Hz that is more work than both iFFTs of the grain combined, and
  // it was the single most expensive thing in a wash-heavy project.
  //
  // Same result, computed as a RUNNING TOTAL: entering bin i, add the neighbour
  // that came into range and subtract the one that left. Cost no longer depends
  // on the width at all -- Spread 150 costs what Spread 1 costs. The window is
  // clipped at both ends and divided by its real width, exactly as the counted
  // version did, so edge bins are averaged over the same neighbours as before.
  i = 0;
  sp > 0 ? (
    // seed the window for bin 0: [0 .. sp]
    sumv = 0; cnt = 0; j = 0;
    loop(min(sp, NBINS - 1) + 1, sumv += mtmp[j]; cnt += 1; j += 1; );
  );
  loop(NBINS,
    sp <= 0 ? ( curmag[i] = mtmp[i]; ) : (
      curmag[i] = sumv / cnt;
      // slide to bin i+1: gain (i+1+sp) if it exists, drop (i-sp) if it existed
      bj2 = i + 1 + sp; bj2 < NBINS ? ( sumv += mtmp[bj2]; cnt += 1; );
      bj2 = i - sp;     bj2 >= 0    ? ( sumv -= mtmp[bj2]; cnt -= 1; );
    );
    i += 1;
  );
  pk = 0; i = 0; loop(NBINS, curmag[i] > pk ? pk = curmag[i]; i += 1; );
  thr = eff_denoise * 0.01 * 0.1 * pk;
  cutbin = floor(eff_lowcut_hz * FFTSIZE / srate);   // eff_ = base + Drift offset
  i = 0;
  loop(NBINS,
    i < cutbin ? ( curmag[i] = 0; ) : ( curmag[i] = max(0, curmag[i] - thr); );
    i += 1;
  );
  // Only the bins this grain's FFT actually reads need a fresh random phase.
  // Was NBINS unconditionally -- another cost that ignored grain size.
  i = 0; loop(GBINS, phase[i] = rand(1)*TWOPI; i += 1; );
  build_spectrum(0);
  rms = 0; i = 0; loop(W, sv = fftwork[2*i]; grainbuf[i] = sv; rms += sv*sv; i += 1; );
  rms = sqrt(rms / W);
  // Slow auto-gain: smooth the grain RMS across grains so loudness is stable and
  // does NOT pump per grain. With the sqrt-Hann constant-power window below,
  // overlapping random-phase grains sum to steady power. Target ~0.07 grain RMS
  // -> ~0.1 output RMS (-20 dBFS). Freeze the smoother on silent grains (empty
  // slot) so switching back doesn't blip loud.
  rms > 0.0000001 ? ( rms_smooth <= 0 ? rms_smooth = rms : rms_smooth += 0.02 * (rms - rms_smooth); );
  gnorm = rms_smooth > 0.0000001 ? (0.07 / rms_smooth) : 0;
  build_spectrum(1);
  i = 0;
  loop(W,
    aw = accpos + i; aw >= ACCLEN ? aw -= ACCLEN;
    accL[aw] += grainbuf[i]   * gnorm * synwin[i];
    accR[aw] += fftwork[2*i]  * gnorm * synwin[i];
    i += 1;
  );
);

// Rebuild ONLY the synthesis grain window (sqrt-Hann, length W = Wash grain).
// CHEAP: no FFT, no YIN, no accumulator clear -- so Wash grain can be dragged
// or AUTOMATED without dropouts (old-length grains finish as new ones start).
// GFFT: the synthesis FFT is sized TO THE GRAIN, not fixed at FFTSIZE.
//
// A grain of W samples cannot carry more spectral detail than W supports, so
// synthesizing FFTSIZE points and then keeping only the first W was buying
// nothing -- it was pure discarded work, and the shorter the grain the more of
// it got thrown away. Worse, cost-per-grain was CONSTANT while grains fire
// every W/4 samples, so shortening the grain multiplied CPU linearly: at the
// bottom of the Wash grain range the wash fired ~800 grains/sec, each paying
// two full 32768-point iFFTs. That is the "even dropouts at short grain"
// symptom -- real-time underrun, not a windowing artifact.
//
// Sizing the FFT to the grain inverts that: short grains become the CHEAPEST
// setting instead of the most expensive, and long grains are unchanged in
// character (at the default grain the old FFT was already longer than the
// grain itself, so the extra resolution was never audible).
//
// GR is the source->target bin stride. The captured spectra stay on the fixed
// FFTSIZE analysis grid; only synthesis resolution adapts.
// Crossfade one per-slot value the same way the spectra are crossfaded.
function sblend(arr, i, j, f) ( arr[i] * (1 - f) + arr[j] * f );

function build_synwin(wlen) local(i) (
  wlen = max(64, min(MAXFFT, floor(wlen)));
  W = wlen; HOP = max(1, floor(W / 4));
  GFFT = 256;
  loop(16, GFFT < W ? GFFT *= 2; );      // bounded: 256 << 16 covers MAXFFT
  GFFT = min(GFFT, FFTSIZE);
  GBINS = GFFT/2 + 1;
  GR = FFTSIZE / GFFT;                   // integer: both are powers of two
  // JSFX ifft() is UNNORMALIZED ("scaled down by 1/size, if used"), so raw grain
  // amplitude tracks GFFT. Folding 1/GFFT into the magnitudes keeps grain level
  // independent of grain size -- without it the slow auto-gain smoother would
  // have to chase a large jump every time GFFT crossed a power of two, i.e.
  // dragging Wash grain would swell and dip. Free: it rides an existing multiply.
  GINV = 1 / GFFT;
  i = 0; loop(W, synwin[i] = sqrt(0.5 - 0.5*cos(TWOPI*i/(W-1))); i += 1; );
);
function clear_accum() local(i) (
  i = 0; loop(ACCLEN, accL[i] = 0; accR[i] = 0; i += 1; );
  accpos = 0; hopcount = 0;
);
// wavetable sine: linear-interpolated lookup of one precomputed period. Only the
// sin() EVALUATION changes; phase accumulators/increments are untouched, so every
// harmonic stays exactly at (n+1)*f0 -- no detune, no inharmonic content. Phase
// accumulators wrap to [0, TWOPI), so fidx lands in [0, WTBL) and the guard sample
// at sintab[WTBL] covers i0 = WTBL-1.
function wtsin(ph) local(fidx, i0, fr) (
  fidx = ph * WTSCALE;
  i0 = floor(fidx); fr = fidx - i0;
  sintab[i0]*(1-fr) + sintab[i0+1]*fr;
);

// Fisher-Yates shuffle of the first n_used slot indices into driftbag. Drift
// draws its next slot from this bag, so it visits every captured slot exactly
// once per cycle (even coverage, random order) rather than a memoryless walk
// that clusters in the middle. Avoids an immediate repeat across the reshuffle
// seam (if the new first slot equals the one just visited, swap it back one).
// Recompute the list of active (unmuted) slot indices. Called every @block
// (cheap: max 8 iterations) and after any capture, so mute toggles land
// immediately. n_active is the count; active_slots[0..n_active-1] are the
// indices. When 0 slots are active, morph goes silent; when 1, it plays that
// slot solo; when 2+, the sequencer walks the active list.
function rebuild_active_slots() local(i) (
  n_active = 0;
  i = 0;
  loop(n_used,
    slot_mute[i] < 0.5 ? (
      active_slots[n_active] = i;
      n_active += 1;
    );
    i += 1;
  );
);

// Position of `slot` in the active list, or -1 if not present. Used by Sweep
// to find where cur_slot sits so it can walk to the next active neighbour.
function active_pos(slot) local(i, pos) (
  pos = -1;
  i = 0;
  loop(n_active, active_slots[i] == slot ? pos = i; i += 1; );
  pos;
);

function shuffle_bag() local(i, j, t) (
  // Shuffle only the ACTIVE (unmuted) slot indices, not raw 0..n_used.
  i = 0; loop(n_active, driftbag[i] = active_slots[i]; i += 1; );
  i = n_active - 1;
  loop(n_active - 1,
    j = floor(rand(i + 1));
    t = driftbag[i]; driftbag[i] = driftbag[j]; driftbag[j] = t;
    i -= 1;
  );
  (n_active > 1 && driftbag[0] == last_slot) ? ( t = driftbag[0]; driftbag[0] = driftbag[1]; driftbag[1] = t; );
);

// Seed the grain window and its FFT size here rather than relying on @block
// reaching the "grain length changed" branch first. In practice it always does
// (last_gsamp starts at 0), but GFFT / GBINS / GR / GINV are now divisors and
// loop counts in the synthesis path -- leaving them at 0 for even one block
// would be a divide-by-zero, so the dependency is made explicit instead of
// inherited from initialization order.
build_synwin(max(64, floor(150 * srate / 1000)));

@slider
// Every slider read into a named global here; nothing downstream references a
// sliderN directly, so the layout can be reordered without desyncing the engine.
cap_slot      = max(0, min(NSLOTS-1, slider1));
// Keep the flag's value: the slot-switch test below needs to know this is the
// first @slider after a load, and the line that consumes it runs before that.
is_first_slider = first_slider;
cap_trig      = slider2; first_slider ? ( cap_last = cap_trig; first_slider = 0; );  // first @slider after load: sync cap_last so a saved-ON Capture-now never fires a silent capture on reload
// --- Per-slot Capture point (nested-selector, like Drift/Ramp targets). The
//     Capture-point slider is now PER SLOT: switching Capture slot saves the
//     old slot's point and loads the new slot's stored point into slider3, so
//     each slot keeps its own by-ear tuning. Editing slider3 writes the current
//     slot. Suppress the @block re-derive on a pure slot-switch (each slot is
//     already analyzed at its own point) by syncing last_cappoint. ---
// The first @slider after a load is NOT a slot switch, however it looks. A
// project saved with Capture slot 3 arrives with last_cap_slot still 0 from
// @init, and treating that as a switch loads slot 3's banks over the sliders --
// which on a v1 project are empty defaults, so the project's real Texture,
// Denoise and Pitch were destroyed before anything could read them. The values
// on screen are what the project saved; take them as given and stamp the slot.
(last_cap_slot != cap_slot && !is_first_slider) ? (
  // Every per-slot value banks with the slot, same as Capture point does.
  slot_voicedb[last_cap_slot] = slider8;
  slot_texture[last_cap_slot] = slider9 * 0.01;
  slot_spread[last_cap_slot] = slider11;
  slot_pitch[last_cap_slot] = slider12;
  slot_width[last_cap_slot] = slider13;
  slot_lowcut[last_cap_slot] = slider14;
  slot_denoise[last_cap_slot] = slider15;
  slot_linger[last_cap_slot] = slider4;            // linger banks with the slot too
  slot_xfade[last_cap_slot]  = slider5;           // crossfade too
  slot_mute[last_cap_slot]   = slider6 > 0.5 ? 1 : 0;   // and mute
  slider4 = slot_linger[cap_slot];
  slider5 = slot_xfade[cap_slot];
  slider6 = slot_mute[cap_slot] > 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
  slider8 = slot_voicedb[cap_slot];
  slider9 = slot_texture[cap_slot] * 100;
  slider11 = slot_spread[cap_slot];
  slider12 = slot_pitch[cap_slot];
  slider13 = slot_width[cap_slot];
  slider14 = slot_lowcut[cap_slot];
  slider15 = slot_denoise[cap_slot];
  sliderchange(-1);   // refresh the displayed values; NOT slider_automate

  slot_cappoint[last_cap_slot] = slider3 * 0.01;   // save the slot we're leaving
  slider3 = slot_cappoint[cap_slot] * 100;         // load the slot we're entering
  slider_automate(slider3);
  last_cap_slot = cap_slot;
  last_cappoint = slot_cappoint[cap_slot];          // no re-derive on switch: slot already analyzed at this point
) : (
  slot_cappoint[cap_slot] = slider3 * 0.01;         // capture a live scrub of the current slot
  slot_linger[cap_slot] = slider4;                 // and a live linger edit
  slot_xfade[cap_slot]  = slider5;                // and a live crossfade edit
  slot_mute[cap_slot]   = slider6 > 0.5 ? 1 : 0; // and a live mute edit
  // a live edit of any per-slot value stamps the slot it belongs to
  slot_voicedb[cap_slot] = slider8;
  slot_texture[cap_slot] = slider9 * 0.01;
  slot_spread[cap_slot] = slider11;
  slot_pitch[cap_slot] = slider12;
  slot_width[cap_slot] = slider13;
  slot_lowcut[cap_slot] = slider14;
  slot_denoise[cap_slot] = slider15;
  last_cap_slot = cap_slot;   // also syncs the first-load case above
);
cap_point01   = slider3 * 0.01;
dry_db_base   = slider7;                                    // base for Input level drift
dry_gain      = slider7 <= -60 ? 0 : pow(10, slider7/20);   // -60 = true silence
voice_db_base = slider8;                                    // base for Voice level drift
voice_gain    = slider8 <= -60 ? 0 : pow(10, slider8/20);
texture       = slider9 * 0.01;                              // 0 voice .. 1 wash
hlevel        = cos(texture * PI * 0.5);                     // equal-power crossfade
wlevel        = sin(texture * PI * 0.5);
grain_ms        = slider10;
spread_hz     = slider11;
pitch_semi    = slider12;                                    // base for Pitch drift
pitch_ratio   = pow(2.0, slider12/12);
stereo_width  = slider13;
voice_detune  = stereo_width * 0.01 * VOICE_DETUNE_MAX;   // voice width via detuned L/R unison
lowcut_hz     = slider14;
// denoise_amt / pitch_semi / voice_db_base / spread_hz / lowcut_hz /
// stereo_width are written here but no longer read: the effective values come
// from the per-slot banks in @sample. Kept so the @slider path still seeds a
// sane hlevel/wlevel before the first sample runs.
denoise_amt   = slider15;
audition_mode = slider16;                                   // 0 focused slot, 1 morph
morph01       = slider17 * 0.01;
automorph_mode = slider18;
automorph_mode != last_automode ? (
  last_automode = automorph_mode; morph_phase = 0;
  drift_primed = 0;   // force Drift to (re)build its shuffle bag on the next sample
  auto_primed = 0;    // and Sweep / Glide to restart their walk
);


// --- Drift target selector save/restore (nested-selector pattern, matching the
//     rest of the suite). Switching slider19 saves sliders 18-21 into the OLD
//     target's bank slot, then loads the NEW target's stored config into the
//     visible sliders. Otherwise it captures live edits to the current target.
//     All targets drift in parallel from @sample regardless of what's selected. ---
sel_target = slider19;
sel_up     = slider20;
sel_down   = slider21;
sel_per    = slider22;
sel_shape  = slider23;
last_target_select != sel_target ? (
  target_drift_up[last_target_select]    = sel_up;
  target_drift_down[last_target_select]  = sel_down;
  target_drift_per[last_target_select]   = sel_per;
  target_drift_shape[last_target_select] = sel_shape;
  slider20 = target_drift_up[sel_target];
  slider21 = target_drift_down[sel_target];
  slider22 = target_drift_per[sel_target];
  slider23 = target_drift_shape[sel_target];
  slider_automate(slider20);
  slider_automate(slider21);
  slider_automate(slider22);
  slider_automate(slider23);
  last_target_select = sel_target;
) : (
  target_drift_up[sel_target]    = sel_up;
  target_drift_down[sel_target]  = sel_down;
  target_drift_per[sel_target]   = sel_per;
  target_drift_shape[sel_target] = sel_shape;
);
// Per-target "is this target being driven at all?" flag — lets @sample skip the
// per-sample effective-value recompute (and keep the exact original CPU/output)
// for any target with no drift configured.
// --- Ramp target selector save/restore (nested-selector, mirrors Drift).
//     slider25 = target; 24 = per-target `by`; 25 = duration; 26 = start delay.
//     slider29 (Engage) is GLOBAL. All targets ride in parallel from @sample. ---
rsel_target = slider25;
rsel_by     = slider26;
rsel_dur    = slider27;
rsel_delay  = slider28;
last_ramp_target != rsel_target ? (
  ramp_by_mem[last_ramp_target]    = rsel_by;
  ramp_dur_mem[last_ramp_target]   = rsel_dur;
  ramp_delay_mem[last_ramp_target] = rsel_delay;
  slider26 = ramp_by_mem[rsel_target];
  slider27 = ramp_dur_mem[rsel_target];
  slider28 = ramp_delay_mem[rsel_target];
  slider_automate(slider26);
  slider_automate(slider27);
  slider_automate(slider28);
  last_ramp_target = rsel_target;
) : (
  ramp_by_mem[rsel_target]    = rsel_by;
  ramp_dur_mem[rsel_target]   = rsel_dur;
  ramp_delay_mem[rsel_target] = rsel_delay;
);
ramp_engaged = slider29;

// Per-target flags. td_active gates the drift-advance loop; mod_active gates the
// effective-value recompute (drift OR ramp configured). A target with neither
// stays exactly at its base value — bit-identical to no modulation.
i = 0; loop(N_TARGETS,
  td_active[i]  = (target_drift_up[i] > 0 || target_drift_down[i] > 0) ? 1 : 0;
  mod_active[i] = (td_active[i] || ramp_by_mem[i] != 0) ? 1 : 0;
  i += 1;
);
// eff_ defaults = base (so the first @sample and any inactive target read base).
eff_spread_hz = spread_hz; eff_lowcut_hz = lowcut_hz; eff_stereo_width = stereo_width;
drift_restart_free = slider24;   // 0 = restart on play (sync), 1 = free-running

@block
// Transport play-edge: immediate runtime setup -- rebuild window, clear the
// accumulator, reset runtime (captures themselves are NOT touched). With
// ext_noinit, @init no longer does this on play, so it's explicit here. The
// heavy spectrum/harmonic re-derive is NO LONGER done unconditionally here --
// it happens only when the analysis is actually stale, which is what stops the
// every-play crackle.
((play_state == 1 || play_state == 5) && (last_ps != 1 && last_ps != 5)) ? (
  build_synwin(floor(grain_ms * srate / 1000));
  clear_accum();
  inpos = 0; rms_smooth = 0; morph_phase = 0;
  // Restart the walk on the play edge. Glide once used to re-arm because the
  // morph phase was zeroed here; now that the modes step slot to slot, the
  // walk state is what has to be cleared or Glide would stay parked on its
  // final slot for every subsequent play.
  auto_primed = 0; drift_primed = 0; sweep_dir = 1; leg_elapsed = 0;
  last_gsamp = floor(grain_ms * srate / 1000); last_cappoint = cap_point01;
  cap_dirty = 0;
  // (Drift reset is handled by its own transport block below — it must also
  //  catch loop-wraps / rewinds, which this capture-engine play-edge does not.)
  // Re-derive ONLY if the analysis is actually stale. In the normal
  // capture-then-play flow the spectra are already valid, so this does NOTHING
  // -- that is what kills the "crackle every time I hit play" (the old code
  // re-analyzed every slot on every play-edge, N heavy FFT+YIN passes crammed
  // into one block). When it IS stale -- a cold project load that hasn't been
  // scrubbed yet, including an offline render from cold -- derive in full here.
  // At the play-edge the accumulator was just cleared (no grains yet), so this
  // lump lands in the silent onset; and offline render has no real-time deadline
  // anyway, so it guarantees the render starts correct from sample zero.
  analysis_valid == 0 ? (
    si2 = 0; loop(n_used, compute_spectrum(si2); analyze_harm(si2); si2 += 1; );
    analysis_valid = 1;
  );
);
last_ps = play_state;

// --- Drift restart (Drift restart slider). "Restart on play" (default): drift
//     jumps to the start of its cycle the moment the transport begins playing
//     from a stop, so multiple tracks reset TOGETHER and their drifts stay in
//     sync (no clashy out-of-phase pitch motion). "Free-running": the transport
//     is ignored and drift evolves continuously — for a loop playing under/over
//     an unbroken drift, or any continuously-evolving texture. A loop repeat is
//     deliberately NOT a restart in either mode (drift flows straight across
//     loop boundaries); own edge state, independent of the capture play-edge. ---
drift_now_playing = (play_state == 1 || play_state == 5);
(drift_now_playing && drift_was_playing == 0) ? (
  // Ramp ALWAYS restarts its ride on transport play (its wind-down begins from
  // the current values each pass) — the suite's Speed-Ramp transport behaviour.
  ri = 0; loop(N_TARGETS, ramp_t_mem[ri] = 0; ramp_delay_elapsed_mem[ri] = 0; ri += 1; );
  // Drift restarts only in Restart-on-play mode (Free-running ignores transport).
  drift_restart_free == 0 ? (
    di = 0; loop(N_TARGETS,
      target_drift_phase[di]  = 0; target_drift_prev[di]  = 0;
      target_drift_curr[di]   = 0; target_drift_offset[di] = 0;
      di += 1;
    );
  );
);
drift_was_playing = drift_now_playing;

// Wash grain -> CHEAP: rebuild only the synthesis grain, immediately, every
// block if it's moving. No re-analysis, no clear -> safe to automate, no drops.
gsamp = floor(grain_ms * srate / 1000);
// Seed every slot's parameter bank from the visible sliders. Consumed HERE and
// not in @slider: on load REAPER applies the slider line and runs @slider BEFORE
// feeding the serialize blob, so a flag raised during @serialize was set after
// its only reader had already run and was never acted on -- every slot kept its
// @init defaults, which meant Texture 50 on a project built at 100 and Pitch 0
// on tracks written at -6 and -18. @block is the first section guaranteed to run
// after both, so the flag is always seen.
seed_slots_from_sliders == 1 ? (
  seed_slots_from_sliders = 0;
  ss = 0;
  loop(NSLOTS,
    slot_linger[ss]  = slider4;
    slot_xfade[ss]   = slider5;
    slot_mute[ss]    = slider6 > 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
    slot_voicedb[ss] = slider8;  slot_texture[ss] = slider9 * 0.01;
    slot_spread[ss]  = slider11;  slot_pitch[ss]   = slider12;
    slot_width[ss]   = slider13; slot_lowcut[ss]  = slider14;
    slot_denoise[ss] = slider15;
    ss += 1;
  );
);

gsamp != last_gsamp ? ( last_gsamp = gsamp; build_synwin(gsamp); );
rebuild_active_slots();   // cheap (max NSLOTS iterations); picks up mute toggles and new captures

// Capture point -> HEAVY (re-FFT + YIN). Debounced so a by-ear scrub re-derives
// once, when it settles, in one lump. (Fresh load is handled at the play-edge
// above -- analysis_valid starts 0 in @init.) NOT an automation target.
cap_point01 != last_cappoint ? ( last_cappoint = cap_point01; cap_dirty = 1; settle = 0; );
cap_dirty ? (
  settle += 1;
  // On settle, re-derive all captured slots in ONE pass (debounced, so a by-ear
  // scrub recomputes once when it stops moving). Deliberately a single lump, not
  // sliced across blocks: one brief glitch during the scrub beats several smaller
  // glitches smeared into the audio you're listening to. Marks the analysis fresh
  // so the play-edge above won't redo it.
  settle >= 4 ? (
    analysis_valid == 0 ? (
      // Cold project load scrubbed before the first play: nothing is derived
      // yet, so derive ALL captured slots -- each at its OWN stored point.
      si2 = 0; loop(n_used, compute_spectrum(si2); analyze_harm(si2); si2 += 1; );
      analysis_valid = 1;
    ) : (
      // Warm: only the focused slot's capture point moved (per-slot now), so
      // re-derive JUST that slot -- scrubbing one slot no longer retunes the
      // others (the bug this fix addresses).
      compute_spectrum(cap_slot); analyze_harm(cap_slot);
    );
    cap_dirty = 0;
  );
);

(cap_trig > 0.5 && cap_last <= 0.5) ? ( capture(cap_slot);
  // a new capture takes the settings you were listening through
  slot_voicedb[cap_slot] = slider8;  slot_texture[cap_slot] = slider9 * 0.01;
  slot_spread[cap_slot]  = slider11;  slot_pitch[cap_slot]   = slider12;
  slot_width[cap_slot]   = slider13; slot_lowcut[cap_slot]  = slider14;
  slot_denoise[cap_slot] = slider15;
  slider2 = 0; cap_trig = 0; sliderchange(slider2); );  // momentary: auto-release Capture-now so it can never be SAVED on (which re-captured silence on every load)
cap_last = cap_trig;

@sample
inbuf[inpos] = (spl0 + spl1) * 0.5;
inpos += 1; inpos >= INRING ? inpos = 0;

// --- Drift: advance each CONFIGURED target and compute its current offset.
//     Period is wall-clock SECONDS (this plugin has no musical clock). Shape
//     math (Sine / Triangle / Random value-noise) matches the rest of the
//     suite. Offset is asymmetric: positive half scales by `up`, negative by
//     `down`. Runs before every consumer below so grain/voice/output all agree. ---
di = 0;
loop(N_TARGETS,
  td_active[di] ? (
    dper = target_drift_per[di];
    dphase = target_drift_phase[di] + 1.0 / max(dper * srate, 1);
    dphase >= 1.0 ? (
      dphase -= 1.0;
      target_drift_shape[di] == 2 ? (
        target_drift_prev[di] = target_drift_curr[di];
        target_drift_curr[di] = rand(2) - 1;   // new random target in [-1,1]
      );
    );
    target_drift_phase[di] = dphase;
    target_drift_shape[di] == 0 ? (
      dshape = sin(TWOPI * dphase);
    ) : target_drift_shape[di] == 1 ? (
      dshape = dphase < 0.25 ? (4*dphase) : dphase < 0.75 ? (2 - 4*dphase) : (4*dphase - 4);
    ) : (
      dshape = target_drift_prev[di] + (target_drift_curr[di] - target_drift_prev[di]) * dphase;
    );
    target_drift_offset[di] = dshape > 0 ? dshape * target_drift_up[di] : dshape * target_drift_down[di];
  );
  di += 1;
);
// --- Ramp: while Engaged, each target with a duration advances its own ride
//     0..1 over that duration, after its own start delay; while Off, all rides
//     freeze and resume. The offset (ride * by) is computed every sample
//     (frozen when not engaged), and folds into the effective values alongside
//     the Drift offset below. ---
ramp_engaged ? (
  ri = 0;
  loop(N_TARGETS,
    ramp_dur_mem[ri] > 0 ? (
      rdelay_samps = ramp_delay_mem[ri] * 60 * srate;
      ramp_delay_elapsed_mem[ri] < rdelay_samps ? (
        ramp_delay_elapsed_mem[ri] += 1;
      ) : (
        ramp_t_mem[ri] += 1.0 / (srate * ramp_dur_mem[ri] * 60);
        ramp_t_mem[ri] > 1.0 ? ramp_t_mem[ri] = 1.0;
      );
    );
    ri += 1;
  );
);
ri = 0; loop(N_TARGETS, ramp_offset_mem[ri] = ramp_t_mem[ri] * ramp_by_mem[ri]; ri += 1; );

// Every auto-morph mode now walks slot to slot, holding each leg for the
// linger of the slot it is LEAVING. Sweep and Glide used to slide a position
// along the slot line at a fixed rate, which structurally could not give two
// steps different lengths; Shuffle already worked this way, so this unifies
// them rather than adding a third behaviour.
automorph_mode > 0.5 ? (
  // Degenerate cases: no active slots at all -> silent pair; one active ->
  // that one solo. The n_active < 2 branch was previously "n_used < 2", but
  // with mute the effective count is n_active.
  n_active < 1 ? ( cur_slot = 0; nxt_slot = 0; xfade = 0; ) :
  n_active < 2 ? ( cur_slot = active_slots[0]; nxt_slot = cur_slot; xfade = 0; ) : (
    automorph_mode == 3 ? (
      // Shuffle: order comes from the bag. Primed lazily -- NOT on mode entry,
      // because on reload that can fire before the captures finish loading
      // (n_used still 0), which stuck cur == nxt on slot 0.
      drift_primed != 1 ? (
        last_slot = -1; shuffle_bag(); bag_pos = 0;
        cur_slot = driftbag[bag_pos]; bag_pos += 1;
        nxt_slot = driftbag[bag_pos]; bag_pos += 1;
        xfade = 0; drift_primed = 1;
      );
    ) : (
      // Sweep and Glide: straight along the ACTIVE slot list.
      auto_primed != 1 ? (
        cur_slot = active_slots[0]; nxt_slot = active_slots[1];
        sweep_dir = 1; xfade = 0; auto_primed = 1;
      );
    );

    // Glide once holds on the final slot; everything else keeps moving.
    // Glide ends when we arrive at the last ACTIVE slot (was: n_used-1).
    (automorph_mode == 2 && cur_slot == active_slots[n_active - 1]) ? (
      xfade = 0; nxt_slot = cur_slot;
    ) : (
      // Slot linger = pure hold time. Slot crossfade = added on top. Leg length
      // is the two summed. The number the user types for linger is what they
      // hear as pure-slot time -- no subtraction, no ratio.
      leg_hold  = max(0, slot_linger[cur_slot]);
      leg_fade  = max(0, slot_xfade[cur_slot]);
      leg_len   = max(0.05, leg_hold + leg_fade);
      leg_elapsed += 1 / srate;
      xfade = leg_elapsed <= leg_hold ? 0 :
              (leg_fade <= 0.0001 ? 1 :
               min(1, (leg_elapsed - leg_hold) / leg_fade));
      leg_elapsed >= leg_len ? (
        cur_slot = nxt_slot; xfade = 0; leg_elapsed = 0;
        automorph_mode == 3 ? (
          bag_pos >= n_active ? ( last_slot = cur_slot; shuffle_bag(); bag_pos = 0; );   // through them all -> reshuffle
          nxt_slot = driftbag[bag_pos]; bag_pos += 1;
        ) : (
          // Sweep bounces at either end of the ACTIVE slot list. Glide
          // reaches here exactly once, on arrival at the last active slot,
          // and the hold branch above catches it on the following sample --
          // with xfade at 0 the crossfade sits fully on cur_slot, so the
          // momentary nxt_slot is never heard.
          cur_pos = active_pos(cur_slot);
          cur_pos < 0 ? cur_pos = 0;   // cur got muted mid-play: snap to start
          (sweep_dir > 0 && cur_pos >= n_active - 1) ? sweep_dir = -1;
          (sweep_dir < 0 && cur_pos <= 0) ? sweep_dir = 1;
          nxt_pos = max(0, min(n_active - 1, cur_pos + sweep_dir));
          nxt_slot = active_slots[nxt_pos];
        );
      );
    );
  );
) : ( eff_morph01 = morph01; );

// Shared slot selection -- BOTH engines read vsi/vsj/vmfr so they always agree.
audition_mode < 0.5 ? (
  // Focused-slot monitor: play exactly the capture slot, ignore morph.
  vsi = cap_slot; vsj = cap_slot; vmfr = 0;
) : automorph_mode > 0.5 ? (
  // Every auto mode: a DIRECT crossfade between the two slots of the current
  // leg, never a position on the slot line. One leg is one crossfade whichever
  // slots it joins -- no whoosh, and nothing in the middle to over-dwell.
  vsi = cur_slot; vsj = nxt_slot; vmfr = xfade;
) : (
  // Manual morph / Sweep / Glide: a position along the fixed slot line, blending
  // the two adjacent slots it sits between.
  vnu = n_used < 1 ? 1 : n_used;
  vmp = eff_morph01 * (vnu - 1);
  vsi = floor(vmp); vmfr = vmp - vsi;
  vsi >= vnu - 1 ? ( vsi = vnu - 1; vmfr = 0; );
  vsj = vsi < vnu - 1 ? vsi + 1 : vsi;
);

// Effective values = the two current slots' settings crossfaded by the same
// morph fraction that crossfades their spectra, THEN Drift wander and Ramp ride
// added on top. This has to sit AFTER the slot choice above, because the base
// is no longer a global -- it moves as the morph moves.
//
// Auditioning a focused slot pins vsi = vsj, so a slot is always heard with
// exactly its own settings; there is no blended state to confuse it with.
sb_i = vsi; sb_j = vsj; sb_f = vmfr;
eff_tex = max(0, min(1, sblend(slot_texture, sb_i, sb_j, sb_f)
                        + (target_drift_offset[0] + ramp_offset_mem[0]) * 0.01));
hlevel = cos(eff_tex * PI * 0.5); wlevel = sin(eff_tex * PI * 0.5);

eff_spread_hz = max(0, min(150, sblend(slot_spread, sb_i, sb_j, sb_f)
                                + target_drift_offset[1] + ramp_offset_mem[1]));

eff_semi = max(-24, min(24, sblend(slot_pitch, sb_i, sb_j, sb_f)
                            + target_drift_offset[2] + ramp_offset_mem[2]));
pitch_ratio = pow(2.0, eff_semi/12);

eff_stereo_width = max(0, min(100, sblend(slot_width, sb_i, sb_j, sb_f)
                                   + target_drift_offset[3] + ramp_offset_mem[3]));
voice_detune = eff_stereo_width * 0.01 * VOICE_DETUNE_MAX;

eff_lowcut_hz = max(0, min(500, sblend(slot_lowcut, sb_i, sb_j, sb_f)
                                + target_drift_offset[4] + ramp_offset_mem[4]));

eff_vdb = max(-60, min(12, sblend(slot_voicedb, sb_i, sb_j, sb_f)
                           + target_drift_offset[5] + ramp_offset_mem[5]));
voice_gain = eff_vdb <= -60 ? 0 : pow(10, eff_vdb/20);

eff_denoise = max(0, min(100, sblend(slot_denoise, sb_i, sb_j, sb_f)
                              + target_drift_offset[6] + ramp_offset_mem[6]));

// Morph and Input level are global, but newly reachable by Drift / Ramp.
mod_active[7] ? (
  eff_morph01 = max(0, min(1, eff_morph01
                   + (target_drift_offset[7] + ramp_offset_mem[7]) * 0.01));
);
mod_active[8] ? (
  eff_dry_db = max(-60, min(12, dry_db_base + target_drift_offset[8] + ramp_offset_mem[8]));
  dry_gain = eff_dry_db <= -60 ? 0 : pow(10, eff_dry_db/20);
);

dryL = spl0 * dry_gain; dryR = spl1 * dry_gain;

// --- wash (spectral) engine: read overlap-add accumulator, refill per hop ---
wL = accL[accpos]; accL[accpos] = 0;
wR = accR[accpos]; accR[accpos] = 0;
accpos += 1; accpos >= ACCLEN ? accpos = 0;
hopcount += 1;
// Skip grain synthesis (gen_grain is HEAVY: two FFTSIZE iFFTs) when the wash is
// inaudible -- the mirror of the voice engine's "skip when Texture is full wash"
// guard below. At Texture 0 (pure voice) wlevel is 0, so wL*wlevel contributes
// nothing anyway; building grains for it was pure wasted CPU -- a real per-grain
// FFT load that could tip a busy project into occasional real-time dropouts
// (the "crackle on every slot, non-clipping" symptom). The accumulator still
// drains via the read-and-clear above, so raising Texture off 0 fades the wash
// back in cleanly over ~one grain. Output is bit-identical while muted.
hopcount >= HOP ? ( hopcount = 0; (have > 0 && wlevel > 0.0001) ? gen_grain(); );

// --- harmonic (voice) engine: TWO morph voices (vsi/vsj), each at its OWN
// captured pitch, crossfaded by morph. Now STEREO: when Stereo width (->
// voice_detune) > 0 the right channel runs a slightly-detuned copy, so L/R beat
// slowly -> real width + a shimmer that softens the robotic edge of pure
// additive harmonics. At width 0 it's the exact original mono path. Skipped
// entirely when the voice is inaudible (Texture at full wash, hlevel ~ 0) --
// that reclaims the whole per-sample harmonic loop when you live on the wash.
(hlevel > 0.0001 && have > 0) ? (
  fA = slot_f0[vsi] * pitch_ratio; normA = slot_hnorm[vsi]; normA <= 0 ? normA = 1;
  fB = slot_f0[vsj] * pitch_ratio; normB = slot_hnorm[vsj]; normB <= 0 ? normB = 1;
  bA = vsi*NHARM; bB = vsj*NHARM;
  voice_detune > 0 ? (
    // Stereo: left slightly flat, right slightly sharp (symmetric, so the
    // perceived pitch centre is unchanged). Separate R phase banks (hphR/hphBR)
    // run at the detuned frequency and drift against the L banks = width.
    fAL = fA*(1-voice_detune); fAR = fA*(1+voice_detune);
    fBL = fB*(1-voice_detune); fBR = fB*(1+voice_detune);
    vvAL = 0; vvAR = 0; vvBL = 0; vvBR = 0; vn = 0;
    loop(NHARM,
      hmA = slot_harm[bA+vn]/normA;
      ((vn+1)*fAL) < srate*0.5 ? ( vvAL += hmA*wtsin(hph[vn]);  );
      ((vn+1)*fAR) < srate*0.5 ? ( vvAR += hmA*wtsin(hphR[vn]); );
      hph[vn]  += TWOPI*(vn+1)*fAL/srate; hph[vn]  >= TWOPI ? hph[vn]  -= TWOPI;
      hphR[vn] += TWOPI*(vn+1)*fAR/srate; hphR[vn] >= TWOPI ? hphR[vn] -= TWOPI;
      hmB = slot_harm[bB+vn]/normB;
      ((vn+1)*fBL) < srate*0.5 ? ( vvBL += hmB*wtsin(hphB[vn]);  );
      ((vn+1)*fBR) < srate*0.5 ? ( vvBR += hmB*wtsin(hphBR[vn]); );
      hphB[vn]  += TWOPI*(vn+1)*fBL/srate; hphB[vn]  >= TWOPI ? hphB[vn]  -= TWOPI;
      hphBR[vn] += TWOPI*(vn+1)*fBR/srate; hphBR[vn] >= TWOPI ? hphBR[vn] -= TWOPI;
      vn += 1;
    );
    hVL = ((1-vmfr)*vvAL + vmfr*vvBL) * 0.08;   // ~match the wash's ~0.1 RMS
    hVR = ((1-vmfr)*vvAR + vmfr*vvBR) * 0.08;
  ) : (
    // Mono (Stereo width 0): the exact original single-bank path, L = R.
    vvA = 0; vvB = 0; vn = 0;
    loop(NHARM,
      ((vn+1)*fA) < srate*0.5 ? ( vvA += (slot_harm[bA+vn]/normA)*wtsin(hph[vn]); );
      hph[vn]  += TWOPI*(vn+1)*fA/srate; hph[vn]  >= TWOPI ? hph[vn]  -= TWOPI;
      ((vn+1)*fB) < srate*0.5 ? ( vvB += (slot_harm[bB+vn]/normB)*wtsin(hphB[vn]); );
      hphB[vn] += TWOPI*(vn+1)*fB/srate; hphB[vn] >= TWOPI ? hphB[vn] -= TWOPI;
      vn += 1;
    );
    hVL = ((1-vmfr)*vvA + vmfr*vvB) * 0.08;
    hVR = hVL;
  );
) : ( hVL = 0; hVR = 0; );

// --- crossfade voice <-> wash (equal-power), gate on having a capture ---
have > 0 ? (
  voutL = hlevel*hVL + wlevel*wL;
  voutR = hlevel*hVR + wlevel*wR;
) : ( voutL = 0; voutR = 0; );
voutL *= voice_gain; voutR *= voice_gain;

spl0 = dryL + voutL;
spl1 = dryR + voutR;

@serialize
// Persist captures across project save/reopen. Save only the RAW audio (source
// of truth) + counts; wash spectrum and harmonic analysis re-derive from slotraw
// on the first @block after load. Magic leads the stream so an old/absent blob
// degrades to "no captures" instead of scrambling state (CLAUDE.md gotcha).
// Magic:
//   7700001 -- v1 blob layout (Auto-morph time global, 6-wide Drift/Ramp banks,
//              no per-slot banks). Read in its own shape; per-slot banks seeded
//              from the visible sliders in @block.
//   7700002 -- v2 Option A layout (linger = full interval, crossfade nested in
//              it). Read as v2, then Slot linger converted on the fly to Option B
//              semantics: new_linger = max(0, old_linger - old_crossfade). This
//              preserves the SOUND of an Option-A-saved project under B.
//   7700003 -- current, Option B layout (linger = pure hold, crossfade added
//              on top). Read straight through.
ser_magic = 7700003;
file_var(0, ser_magic);
(ser_magic == 7700003 || ser_magic == 7700002 || ser_magic == 7700001) ? (
  ser_v1  = ser_magic == 7700001;
  ser_v2a = ser_magic == 7700002;   // old Option A; needs linger conversion below
  // A v2 blob's banks are authoritative -- cancel the fresh-instance seed.
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && !ser_v1) ? ( seed_slots_from_sliders = 0; );
  n_ser_targets = ser_v1 ? 6 : N_TARGETS;
  file_var(0, have);
  file_var(0, n_used);
  // Save/restore only the slots actually captured (n_used * MAXFFT), not the
  // full NSLOTS store -- so raising the slot count doesn't bloat the project
  // file with empty slots, and it scales with what's really in use. Backward
  // compatible: an old save that stored the full 4-slot block still restores
  // its captures (file_mem reads only n_used*MAXFFT, the leading slots, and
  // stops -- the trailing bytes were always empty tail slots anyway).
  file_mem(0, slotraw, n_used*MAXFFT);

  // --- Drift config, APPENDED at the end (safe without a magic bump). A
  //     pre-Drift project has the same 7700001 magic but no drift bytes; these
  //     reads run past EOF, and REAPER leaves the destination unchanged on a
  //     short read -- so old projects keep their captures and get default drift.
  //     Inserting mid-stream would misalign; appending is EOF-safe. ---
  file_mem(0, target_drift_up,    n_ser_targets);
  file_mem(0, target_drift_down,  n_ser_targets);
  file_mem(0, target_drift_per,   n_ser_targets);
  file_mem(0, target_drift_shape, n_ser_targets);
  file_var(0, last_target_select);

  // --- Ramp config, appended after Drift. EOF-safe: a pre-Ramp project (drift
  //     only, or captures only) reads past EOF here and keeps default ramp. ---
  file_mem(0, ramp_by_mem,    n_ser_targets);
  file_mem(0, ramp_dur_mem,   n_ser_targets);
  file_mem(0, ramp_delay_mem, n_ser_targets);
  file_var(0, last_ramp_target);

  // --- Per-slot Capture point, appended after Ramp (EOF-safe append; no magic
  //     bump, same as Drift/Ramp were added). MIGRATION for projects saved
  //     before this field: they have no bytes here, so the read runs past EOF
  //     and REAPER leaves slot_cappoint unchanged. We detect that on READ with a
  //     sentinel dropped into slot 0 just before the read -- if it survives, the
  //     field was absent, so we seed every slot from the OLD global capture point
  //     (slider3). Pre-fix, all slots were analyzed at that one point, so this
  //     reproduces the old sound exactly. On WRITE (file_avail < 0) the sentinel
  //     is never set, so the real values are saved. ---
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_cappoint[0] = -999; );
  file_mem(0, slot_cappoint, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_cappoint[0] == -999) ? (
    seed_cp = slider3 * 0.01;
    scp = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_cappoint[scp] = seed_cp; scp += 1; );
  );

  // A v1 blob ends after Capture point. Seed the banks v2 added, and ask
  // @slider to fill the per-slot parameter banks from the visible sliders on its
  // next run -- under v1 those WERE a single global applied to every slot, so
  // copying them across all slots reproduces exactly how the project sounded.
  // Deferred to @slider because load order between the two sections is not
  // guaranteed and the slider values may not have arrived yet.
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && ser_v1) ? (
    sv1 = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_linger[sv1] = 4; slot_xfade[sv1] = 4; slot_mute[sv1] = 0; sv1 += 1; );
    sv1 = 6; loop(N_TARGETS - 6,
      target_drift_up[sv1] = 0; target_drift_down[sv1] = 0;
      target_drift_per[sv1] = 30; target_drift_shape[sv1] = 0;
      ramp_by_mem[sv1] = 0; ramp_dur_mem[sv1] = 0; ramp_delay_mem[sv1] = 0;
      sv1 += 1; );
    seed_slots_from_sliders = 1;
  );

  // --- Per-slot dwell, appended after Capture point. Same EOF-safe shape: a
  //     project saved before dwell existed has no bytes here, so the read runs
  //     past EOF and the sentinel survives -> seed every slot to even (1), which
  //     is exactly how those projects already sound. ---
  ser_v1 ? 0 : ( file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_linger[0] = -999; ) );
  file_mem(0, slot_linger, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_linger[0] == -999) ? (
    sdw = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_linger[sdw] = 4; sdw += 1; );
  );

  // Slot crossfade: appended after Slot linger. EOF-safe -- a project saved
  // before this field existed leaves the sentinel untouched, and we seed
  // slot_xfade to match slot_linger so those projects sound exactly as they
  // did (pure crossfade, no hold). New / live-edited slots override as usual.
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_xfade[0] = -999; );
  file_mem(0, slot_xfade, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_xfade[0] == -999) ? (
    sxf = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_xfade[sxf] = slot_linger[sxf]; sxf += 1; );
  );

  // --- Per-slot parameter banks, appended. Same sentinel migration as the
  //     per-slot Capture point: absent bytes leave the seeded defaults. ---
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_voicedb[0] = -999 );
  file_mem(0, slot_voicedb, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_voicedb[0] == -999) ? (
    sps = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_voicedb[sps] = 0.0; sps += 1; );
  );
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_texture[0] = -999 );
  file_mem(0, slot_texture, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_texture[0] == -999) ? (
    sps = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_texture[sps] = 0.5; sps += 1; );
  );
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_spread[0] = -999 );
  file_mem(0, slot_spread, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_spread[0] == -999) ? (
    sps = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_spread[sps] = 0.0; sps += 1; );
  );
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_pitch[0] = -999 );
  file_mem(0, slot_pitch, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_pitch[0] == -999) ? (
    sps = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_pitch[sps] = 0.0; sps += 1; );
  );
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_width[0] = -999 );
  file_mem(0, slot_width, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_width[0] == -999) ? (
    sps = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_width[sps] = 50.0; sps += 1; );
  );
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_lowcut[0] = -999 );
  file_mem(0, slot_lowcut, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_lowcut[0] == -999) ? (
    sps = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_lowcut[sps] = 0.0; sps += 1; );
  );
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_denoise[0] = -999 );
  file_mem(0, slot_denoise, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_denoise[0] == -999) ? (
    sps = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_denoise[sps] = 0.0; sps += 1; );
  );

  // Option A -> B conversion. Under A, slot_linger was the total leg length
  // (hold + fade combined) and slot_xfade was the fade portion. Under B,
  // slot_linger is the pure hold and slot_xfade is the added fade -- so an
  // Option-A-saved project's linger has the crossfade baked in and needs
  // subtracting out to keep the same sound.
  ser_v2a ? (
    cv = 0;
    loop(NSLOTS,
      slot_linger[cv] = max(0, slot_linger[cv] - slot_xfade[cv]);
      cv += 1;
    );
  );

  // Slot mute: appended at the VERY END of the v2 section, after every other
  // per-slot bank. Was originally inserted between slot_xfade and slot_voicedb,
  // which shifted every subsequent bank's read by 32 bytes and corrupted
  // Rozaya's saved v2 project (Texture read as 10000, Stereo width read as
  // 500, etc.). Serialize fields for existing v2 magic values MUST NOT be
  // inserted mid-stream -- new fields append at the end so old blobs read
  // past EOF and get their EOF-safe defaults. If we ever need mid-stream
  // additions, bump the magic and gate on the version.
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? ( slot_mute[0] = -999; );
  file_mem(0, slot_mute, NSLOTS);
  (file_avail(0) >= 0 && slot_mute[0] == -999) ? (
    sm = 0; loop(NSLOTS, slot_mute[sm] = 0; sm += 1; );
  );

  // TRACK-DUPLICATE FIX (CLAUDE.md nested-selector gotcha). On READ (load /
  // duplicate) file_avail(0) >= 0; on WRITE (save / undo) it's < 0. @serialize
  // is the one section guaranteed to run on both load AND duplicate, so after
  // restoring the banks we force the visible Drift AND Ramp sliders back to the
  // restored selected targets -- correcting any transient @slider clobber and
  // restoring the "visible slider == bank[selected]" invariant. sliderchange
  // (NOT slider_automate) here -- automate would write automation on load.
  file_avail(0) >= 0 ? (
    slider20 = target_drift_up[last_target_select];
    slider21 = target_drift_down[last_target_select];
    slider22 = target_drift_per[last_target_select];
    slider23 = target_drift_shape[last_target_select];
    slider26 = ramp_by_mem[last_ramp_target];
    slider27 = ramp_dur_mem[last_ramp_target];
    slider28 = ramp_delay_mem[last_ramp_target];
    // Per-slot Capture point: force slider3 to the restored slot's stored point,
    // and sync last_cap_slot so the first @slider doesn't mistake load for a
    // slot-switch (which would save the visible point into the wrong slot).
    cps = max(0, min(NSLOTS-1, slider1));
    last_cap_slot = cps;
    slider3 = slot_cappoint[cps] * 100;
    // The per-slot banks are only authoritative when they were actually READ.
    //
    // On a v1 project they have NOT been filled yet -- v1 stored no per-slot
    // data, and the seed from the visible sliders is deferred to @block because
    // @slider has already run by this point. Forcing the sliders from them here
    // wrote the @init defaults straight over the project's real values: Texture
    // became 50 on a project saved at 100, Denoise 0 against 25, Pitch 0 against
    // -5.5. @block then seeded the banks from those clobbered sliders, so the
    // whole instance collapsed to defaults with only the captures surviving.
    //
    // For a v1 load the SLIDERS are the source of truth and must be left alone;
    // for a v2 load the banks are, and the sliders follow them as before.
    ser_v1 ? 0 : (
      slider4 = slot_linger[cps];
    slider5 = slot_xfade[cps];
    slider6 = slot_mute[cps] > 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
      slider8 = slot_voicedb[cps];
      slider9 = slot_texture[cps] * 100;
      slider11 = slot_spread[cps];
      slider12 = slot_pitch[cps];
      slider13 = slot_width[cps];
      slider14 = slot_lowcut[cps];
      slider15 = slot_denoise[cps];
    );

    sliderchange(-1);
  );
);
